            <ArticleTitle>Numular headache: a coin-shaped cephalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1678-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Numular headache is a chronic, mild to moderate, pressurelike pain in a circumscribed cranial area of approximately 2 to 6 cm in diameter. Pain usually is limited to the parietal region, although it may appear in any cranial site. It is a benign process of usually unknown origin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
